    "title": "Confirmed lineups for Tottenham vs Atletico Madrid",
    "text": "Tottenham vs Atletico, 2025/26 Champions League last 16, second leg, 18/03/2026, lineups. BeSoccer Check out the confirmed lineups for the second leg of the Champions League last 16 tie between Spurs and Atletico Madrid at the Tottenham Hotspur Stadium, which kicks off at 21:00 CET. Tottenham host Atletico Madrid in London for the second leg of their Champions League round of 16 tie, facing the daunting task of overturning a three-goal deficit after the English side were thrashed 5-2 by the ‘Colchoneros’ in the first leg. The Spaniards needed just the first 22 minutes of the first leg to score four goals and all but seal the tie, following blunders by goalkeeper Kinsky on his debut, who was replaced in the 17th minute by Vicario. Porro reduced the deficit before Julian Alvarez added a fifth in the second half, although Solanke found the net and narrowed the gap minutes later. Spurs face an uphill battle, and at one of the lowest points in their recent history in terms of results, meaning the ‘Colchoneros’ are favourites to progress to the quarter-finals. Confirmed lineups for the clash Tottenham XI: Vicario, Dragusin, Xavi, Tel, Gray, Romero (C), Pedro Porro, Spence, Sarr, Van der Ven, Kolo Muani. Atletico Madrid XI: Musso, Molina, Le Normand, Hancko, Ruggeri, Giuliano, Llorente, Cardoso, Lookman, Griezmann, Alvarez.",
